{"name":"Golden Boy","hex":"#ffdd44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden boy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young man who has become unusually successful at an early age.","A favored youth, held in high esteem by others, and for whom there are high hopes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_boy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Boy (Anikushin)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Boy is a sculpture created by Mikhail Anikushin, a celebrated Soviet sculptor honored with the titles People's Artist of the USSR and recipient of both the Lenin Prize and I. E. Repin State Prizes of the RSFSR. The work was conceived as part of the larger Memorial to the Heroic Defenders of Leningrad, dedicated to those who endured the siege of the city during World War II. The memorial itself was unveiled in 1975 in Leningrad and was designed by architects Valentin Kamensky and Sergei Speransky. The model for the sculpture was Anikushin's own grandson, Adrian Anikushin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Boy_(Anikushin)","wikidata":"Q105490805"},{"title":"Spirit of Communication","blocks":[{"text":"Spirit of Communication is the formal name for the statue by Evelyn Beatrice Longman originally called Genius of Telegraphy. The statue has been the symbol of AT&T since their commission was completed in 1916. It is also known informally as the Golden Boy statue and formerly as Genius of Electricity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/AT%26T%27s_Spirit_of_Communications_%28Golden_Boy%29_sculpture_in_its_current_location_outside_of_AT%26T%27s_headquarters_in_Dallas%2C_Texas.jpg/330px-AT%26T%27s_Spirit_of_Communications_%28Golden_Boy%29_sculpture_in_its_current_location_outside_of_AT%26T%27s_headquarters_in_Dallas%2C_Texas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_of_Communication","wikidata":"Q1534847"},{"title":"Golden Boy (award)","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden Boy is an award established by Italian sports newspaper Tuttosport, that is given by sports journalists to a young male footballer playing in Europe perceived to have been the most impressive during a calendar year. All nominees must be under the age of 21 and play in a European nation's top tier. Apart from the main award, an additional one, Golden Boy Web, is decided by online users."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Doue_asse_psg_2425.png/330px-Doue_asse_psg_2425.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Boy_(award)","wikidata":"Q1588911"},{"title":"Boy","blocks":[{"text":"A boy is a young male human. The term is commonly used for a child or an adolescent. When a male human reaches adulthood, they are usually described as a man."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg/330px-Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy","wikidata":"Q3010"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/%D0%9C%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%83%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%82_%D0%B3%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BC_%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%89%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BC_%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B0_4.jpg/500px-%D0%9C%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%83%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%82_%D0%B3%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BC_%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%89%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BC_%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B0_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/%D0%9C%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%83%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%82_%D0%B3%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BC_%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%89%D